I'd appreciate some advice on early-game pacifism and on the
particular problem stated below.

I am playing a Level 1 Samurai, I am currently at dlvl 1 with a large
dog as a pet. In "Maniac's Ascension Guide (3.4.2)", which I found on
the internet, I read about playing with a pacifist conduct in the
early levels. The idea is to make it to the Minetown while still at
level 1 and in order to buy cheap protection from the priest there.

I decided to try it, and by now I have killed a couple of characters
in the progress of trying it out. I do like playing this way, it makes
me more careful when exploring a dungeon and I hope to make being
careful a habit this way, even when I am finally going to gain levels
by killing monsters directly.

One problem I am facing is that it seems nearly impossible to survive
the Gnomish Mines in this style. The large space and especially the
darkness make it a hazard without proper equipment (and I don't want
to go on with this forever in order to find that equipment). I read
some FAQ about the pacifist style and I tried to play a gnomish healer
once. That one did indeed make to to the mine town---at clvl 2 due to
a few accidental kills---until it got killed because of bad luck. I'd
try it again, but I don't like the idea of being forced to play a
particular race/class combination. I'd like to try a human samurai.

